# Coach speech (European Portuguese): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "tu" and is male ("Obrigado pela partida"); the
# player's gender is unknown: no adjective or participle about the player ("pronto", "atento"):
# verbs ("ganhaste", "estavas a ganhar", "já podes passar ao nível ...") or nouns instead.
# Portugal's past tense for what happened in the game ("ganhaste", "jogámos", "empatámos").
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}, {opening} (written to fit every line that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   with their article ("a abertura", "o meio-jogo", "o final"); never after
#                       de / em: common.lang gives "{text:em}" = "na abertura", "{text:de}".
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement said after "Empate, {text}." ("por repetição", "por acordo").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase in lower case, no full stop ("vigiar os ataques
#                       duplos"), said after a colon or after "pensa em" (no article to merge).
#   appraisal.level.*   the level name in « », said after "nível": "passar ao nível «Principiante»".
#   {opening:def}       the opening's name with its article ("a Defesa Siciliana"), as an object;
#                       {opening} alone (the citation name) after a colon.
# Move numbers: "no lance {n}", "até ao lance {crit_no}" (a bare number is masculine).
# Accuracy: "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "oitenta e cinco por cento"), at every level.
# Counts: "{n:piece}", "{n:captured}" = "3 peças capturadas", "{n:capture}", "{m:check}" = "2 xeques",
# "{n:time}" = "2 vezes", "{n:best_move}" = "5 melhores lances"; "de seguida" = in a row.
# "Lances forçantes" = forcing moves (checks, captures, threats).

